# The Bandit Baron's say, before the last fight of Act 3. Fired once by
# MapComponent_TSC_BaronParley the first time a colonist stands in sight of
# him on the keep map. He is never lured into the cellars (the lure skips
# his kind), so he is always here, on his gold, for this.
#
# Every exit is the fight. What the scene offers is exposition, one Insight
# read on the man, and one Persuasion throw over his head at his men:
# success leaves the remaining garrison Shaken for the vault fight.
#
# {PLAYER} is whoever walked into his hall first.

dialogue TSC_Dialogue_BaronParley

== start ==
The Baron does not stand. He sits above the hoard on a camp chair worn to the shape of him, sword flat across his knees: a big man gone grey at the temples, in plate he wears as easily as a shirt. He watches {PLAYER} pick a path through his gold with the expression of a man checking a bill he already knows the total of.

"Five years," he says. "Five years I flew banners in these hills. Hanged thieves. Kept the roads. More than any crown ever did for this country, and what does this country send me... what are you, exactly. Adventurers."

* "Thieves hanging thieves is still thieves." -> thieves
* "We came for what's under your gold, not for you." -> shard
* [Say nothing. Let him talk.] -> talk

== thieves ==
He laughs once, without much in it.

"Aye. And a king is a bandit whose grandfather won. I have read a book, whatever they sing of me." He rolls his shoulders, and the grey plate moves with him like cloth and makes no sound at all, which plate has no business doing. "I took this keep off men worse than me. Ask Thornden whether the tithe was smaller under the old lord. Ask them which of us rode down their sons for sport."

The eyes are tired and perfectly steady.

* "We came for what's under your gold." -> shard
* [Enough words.] -> resolve

== talk ==
"No banner, no writ, no demands read at the gate." He nods slowly, as if a suspicion has been confirmed. "So it's the pile you want. Everyone wants the pile. You are just the first to get this far, which makes you the first I have had to say this to out loud."

He leans forward.

"The old kingdom is not coming back. Somebody was going to hold these hills. It was me, and I held them better than the memory of a dead king ever did. Whatever you do in the next hour, that part stays true."

* "We came for one thing in that pile, and it isn't gold." -> shard
* [Enough words.] -> resolve

== shard ==
For the first time something moves behind his face that is not pre-calculated.

"So that's what it is." Quiet, almost to himself. "There is a thing in that pile I do not sell. Tried twice. Both buyers died on the road, and both times the thing came back with the men I sent after it. It hums, some nights. My dreams have run cold for five years, and I have slept worse every year I owned more gold."

A hand goes to his breastplate, unconscious as a tic.

"The plate came up out of that pile too. It stopped weighing anything the second winter. I told myself that was the smith's genius." A short breath through the nose. "I am not a stupid man. I just wanted the armor."

He stands at last, and the sword comes up with him, and his voice comes back to full parade volume.

"Take the cursed thing. That piece you would not have to kill me for. But the rest is my men's blood and my five years, and that you will pay for properly."

* [Read the man before the blades come out.] -> resolve
    check Insight 7 -> afraid | resolve
* [It ends the same way.] -> resolve

== afraid ==
Under the iron the reading is plain. This is not a last stand for gold. He has been afraid of the thing in his counting room for years, and he would rather die as the Bandit Baron than live as the man who slept beside it and then handed it over for nothing.

* [Give him the death he picked.] -> resolve

== resolve ==
Around the hall, the last of the Iron Brand set their feet: men on the stairs, men at the doors, steel out. Every one of them is watching the Baron and the company by turns, thinking the same thoughts the whole keep has been thinking since the gate.

There is a beat where the room could still be spoken to.

* "Your Baron dies for a haunted trinket. The Brand doesn't have to die with him. Anyone still standing when it's done walks out of these hills." -> spoken
    check Persuasion 8 -> broken | unmoved
* [Let the steel answer.] -> fight

== spoken ==
The words go out over the Baron's head to the men on the stairs.

* [And now the steel.] -> fight

== broken ==
Nobody drops a sword. Nobody was ever going to drop a sword in front of him. But the words land where the Baron cannot see them land: a grip shifted, a glance traded across the hall, half a step backward at the doors. The Brand will fight for their Baron.

They have just stopped planning to die for him.

* [To arms.] -> end
    do demoralize(); grant_xp(50); flag(TSC_BaronParleyDone)

== unmoved ==
"They heard the same offer twice already," the Baron says, level. "Once from the guild's men, once from the company I took this keep from. The men who took those offers are the reason the road here was so quiet."

Nothing moves in the hall except firelight.

* [To arms.] -> end
    do grant_xp(50); flag(TSC_BaronParleyDone)

== fight ==
"Well then," the Baron says, and sets his feet on his own gold.

The last of the Iron Brand answers him from the walls.

* [To arms.] -> end
    do grant_xp(50); flag(TSC_BaronParleyDone)
